<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 1.3 Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept id="t00176">
	<title>High Beam Assist setting</title>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>high beam assist (HBA) 
					<indexterm>setting</indexterm>
				</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<table frame="none" colsep="1" rowsep="1" outputclass="formatc_none">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="1" rowsep="1" outputclass="formatc">
				<colspec colnum="1" colname="1" colwidth="53*"/>
				<colspec colnum="2" colname="2" colwidth="47*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="0">
						<entry colname="1" colsep="0">
							<fig>
								<figgroup>
									<image href="../../images/N_TK25Z042_E.eps" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="2">
							<ol outputclass="callout">
								<li>
									<p> <uicontrol>Lights</uicontrol> </p>
								</li>
								<li>
									<p> <uicontrol>HBA (High Beam Assist)</uicontrol> </p>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>With the <term translate="no">EV</term> button in the <term translate="no">ON</term> position, select <menucascade><uicontrol>Settings</uicontrol><uicontrol>Vehicle</uicontrol><uicontrol>Lights</uicontrol><uicontrol>HBA (High Beam Assist)</uicontrol></menucascade> from the Vehicle Settings menu to turn on High Beam Assist and deselect to turn off the function.</p>
		<note type="warning">
			<p>For your safety, adjust your high beam settings only after parking the vehicle at a safe location.</p>
		</note>
	</conbody>
</concept>